    "reviewed_associations": [
      "Seven blessing formal pages agree on one ranged Volatile implementation and the two actual marks. Tier, localization, percentage, compatibility, source and trait pages cross-link consistently.",
      "The shared map has exactly two Volatile rows, for plasmagun_p1_m1 and plasmagun_p1_m2. Both use the same exact trait id, trait item and category. The Plasma Gun reverse index links both marks to the same trait page.",
      "The catalog, ranged index, weapon reverse page, source index and translation glossary point to consistent names and locations. The image receipt verifies icon 154, path, attachment and image hash.",
      "Canonical config and extension draft agree on id, kind, variant and binding counts, effect summary, exact trait id, icon fields and not_verified faster status. The frozen agent trio hashes remain unchanged."
    ],
    "reviewed_deltas": [
      "The I-IV own values and actual SteppedStatBuff wrapper agree: charge_up_time -0.025/-0.03/-0.035/-0.04 per effective heat-derived step; wrapper computes n=round(5*(1-clamp01((h-.1)/.9))) and clamps 0..5. Held-slot is preserved; reload_state and vent_overheat are excluded by the not-reloading predicate; cached heat can change the step count during charge.",
      "Both actual marks select the M1-named direct and brace charge templates; M2-specific duration templates are defined but not selected. The interpolation examples identify D0 as resolved charge_duration, not a measured Mark time.",
      "Direct-route threshold is independently confirmed: min_charge=.05, fully_charged_charge_level and ActionCharge max_charge=.525, zero delay, and positive-time start from 0. The target factor is (.525-.05)/(1-.05)=.5. At D0=.80, IV three steps and fixed h=.46, duration parameter .80 to .704 and auto-fire threshold time .400 to .352 seconds. For q=.20, threshold .480 to .432 seconds, a 10% reduction over q-only.",
      "The threshold derivation requires fixed heat/cache, zero delay, no interruption, and a reachable threshold. The direct template declares limit_max_charge_to_ammo_clip, but overload_charge dispatches to ActionOverloadCharge extending ActionCharge; only ActionChargeAmmo consumes that field, so no ammo clipping applies on the actual route. The direct action auto maps fully_charged to charged_enough then action_shoot. Brace uses a distinct template and release chain, so the direct half-duration factor is not reused.",
      "Damage prose is bounded: charge_up_time adds no direct damage multiplier; at the same charge level and other conditions it adds no separate shot damage, while faster progress may change charge level at the same elapsed time.",
      "Four RAW tiers are reconstructed with formatter values and no-space-after-placeholder text; the RAW trailing ASCII space is explicitly annotated and not left as Markdown trailing whitespace. Charge Speed / charge speed labels are not called an explicit reciprocal-rate contradiction."
    ],
